{
 "name": "sign_faces",
 "_doc": "ledger 0096 \u2014 MUTCD regulatory / warning faces and Denver street-name blades, generated by tools/make_sign_faces.py. Nothing here is placed on a track.",
 "uv_layout": "the texture is the sign's bounding rectangle edge to edge: u 0..1 left to right, v 0..1 bottom to top, as the reader sees it; resampled to a power of two each way (texels not square); alpha 0 outside the outline with the face's edge colour bled under it. The sign_plate_*.obj meshes carry exactly these UVs on object FACE.",
 "needs_from_engine": "sign plates must keep their UVs through the prep (PLAN \u00a74b engine work 8); a pbr.TEXTURES row per face (or one per material class with a per-face texture) and SIGNBACK -> solid_metal_grey.png; alpha test only if a rectangle is used where the outline is not one",
 "accuracy": "sizes are the MUTCD's single-lane conventional-road sizes (scale the plate where Table 2B-1 gives the larger multi-lane size); layouts are drawn from knowledge of the standard signs, not measured off the Standard Highway Signs sheets; the letters approximate the FHWA Standard Alphabets",
 "mounting": {
  "bottom_above_walk_m": 2.1336,
  "from_kerb_face_m": 0.6096,
  "source": "MUTCD 2A.18, 2A.19"
 },
